ef like a few sentences  on who the character is and in that  first round that's kind of okay because  I think one of the things that let me  make peace with the audition process was  the idea that they're looking for you or  they're not you know you're you're right  or you're not and I remember one of the  main pieces of feedback I used to get  was you know he's just not the guy and  which is a really frustrating bit of  feedback to get because you don't really  know what that means but it absolutely  makes sense and having friends who are  on the other side of the camera you know  that they tell me a lot of the time the  best actor doesn't get the job it's just  someone who is right for the part  and very often in that first round of  self-types whatever it is when they've  cast a wide net they're just looking for  people who fit the archetype or whatever  it is they're looking for the character  I know nothing about the casting process  that's how I've justified it in my mind  but don't worry too much about that you  know whatever it is you're working with  whether it's just the scene or a few  sentences of a character by ogle  whatever it might be just do your best  with what you've got and you'll have  your take on end they'll like it what  they want you'll be fine either way  I've been we've all been there you know  it's really really hard when the phone  isn't ringing and you you feel like you  have nothing to do because you stop  feeling like an actor you feel like  someone who's just you know on the couch  or you're doing your whatever the other  job is you're I was folding clothes you  know at a store and that sucks it's  really horrible because you sort of lose  touch with that person who was excited  and passionate about it and I think  that's the main thing is I got to a  point where I was really upset going to  the movies which is my favorite thing to  do in the whole world because I used to  think I'll just never get there I'll  never be there and tha